ch I doubtless received from  God and then he talks about how God  would not set him up to be deceived so  how is he deceived them well this this  whole business of thinking about where  human being fits in is part of that that  picture of answering this question well  how do I actually go wrong so he's going  to talk about two ideas that he has that  he's had the entire time and now he's  managed to bring to light over the  course of his meditations and which he's  now going to look at more closely in  order to understand where he fits him so  he talks about having a real and  positive you could translate real as  actual if you want a real and positive  idea of God in meditation 3 he talked  about this in terms of actually  providing a proof for God's existence  this this idea is something like a mark  that the workman places upon his product  and the product here is the human mind  so we have an idea of God according to  Descartes that is within our mind so  what is this real and positive idea of  God it's very important actually that we  stress this notion of the being a  positive idea because in some of the  objections some of the commentators are  going to say oh you know you talk about  this infinite being but your your notion  of infinity is basically just like a  primitive idea you're taking away all  sorts of limitations and then you you  have this kind of fuzzy concept in your  mind Descartes is saying no no no I have  an idea of God as a being as he says a  supremely perfect being in other places  he'll talk about this  as a being lacking none of the  perfections of being possessing all of  the perfections and we might want to  think for just a moment what is a  perfection a perfection is something  that it is better to be than not to be  that's you know not take hearts actual  formulation that goes all the way back  to Anselm of Canterbury discussing the  divine attributes but I think it's  perfectly apt right here to think of it  in that way so anything